title: Sandbox Lifecycle Consistency and Recovery Tasks
status: draft
created: 2026-11-16
author: adrian
items[26]{id,title,description,criteria,complexity,effort,dependencies,refs}:
  T-001,"[x] Add paused, create-mode and teardown contract types","Add `Error::Paused { name }` with a message naming `litterbox resume <name>` and map it to `FailureClass::Conflict`. Add `CreateMode { Fresh, ReuseExisting }` to `CreateRequest` and set `Fresh` in every existing constructor and fixture. Add `Teardown { compute_stopped, state_paths, detail }` and change `Backend::delete` to return it. Update Docker and TestBackend to compile with the new signatures, and update `sandbox/mapping.rs` documentation so conflict covers a taken name and a paused state.","The workspace builds. A paused error reports exit class 4 and MCP surface class invalid params. Every `CreateRequest` constructor names a mode. Every `Backend` implementation returns `Teardown` from delete. Existing tests compile and the contract tests for class mapping pass.","medium","3-5h",,"paused-class-parity,neutral-failure-classes,backward-compatibility"
  T-002,"[x] Add the version-tolerant pid probe","Add a small `RecordedPids` value in `payload.rs` that reads only the launcher and sandbox pids and their start times, whatever the payload version. Change `validate` to probe those first: a gone pid is `Absent`; a live pid with an unsupported or unreadable payload is `Unavailable`, not `Missing`; a payload with no readable pid is `Unavailable`. Do not let the probe feed a join, a signal or a cgroup write.","A version 1 payload with a dead pid validates as Absent and inspect reports Missing. A version 1 payload with a live pid validates as Unavailable. A payload with no readable pid validates as Unavailable. A version 2 payload takes the existing full-validation path unchanged. Unit tests cover all four cases.","medium","3-5h","T-001","no-payload-dependence,unreadable-payload-with-workspace,state-directory-corrupt"
  T-003,"[x] Add orchestrator outcome and inspection types","Add `orchestrator/outcome.rs` with `Recovery`, `Performed<T>`, `InspectionReport` and `Deletion`. `InspectionReport` carries either an `Inspection` or a status-only report whose status is `SandboxStatus::Unknown` or `SandboxStatus::Error` with a reason. Change `create`, `exec`, `upload`, `download` and `snapshot` to return `Performed<T>`, and update `SandboxIo` and every call site so the crate compiles.","A successful operation returns `Performed` with no recovery. A recovered operation returns exactly one `Recovery`. `InspectionReport` can carry Unknown and Error and is serialisable where MCP needs it. `cargo check -p agentkit-litterbox` passes.","medium","4-6h","T-001","recovery-warning,unknown-status,neutral-failure-classes"
  T-004,"[x] Serialise repair per sandbox","Add `orchestrator/lock.rs` with a per-project-per-name guard. It creates `<records_dir>/.locks`, takes an in-process async guard keyed by name, then takes `flock(LOCK_EX)` on `<name>.lock` in a blocking task. Hold the guard from the status re-check through the record write. Add a non-unix fallback that uses the in-process guard alone.","Two concurrent calls for the same missing sandbox result in one repair and one observation of active. A lock is released on normal return and when the task is dropped. The lock directory is ignored by record enumeration. A unit test exercises contention at the lock seam.","medium","3-5h","T-001","repair-serialised,atomic-repair,no-new-dependency,concurrent-calls,concurrent-repair-single-holder"
  T-005,"[x] Split create and add the ensure-live gate","Split `create` into branch creation, provisioning resolution and compute creation. Add `Sandboxes::ensure_live(name, policy)` that loads the record, selects the owning backend, inspects, and returns active, refuses paused when the policy says so, repairs missing, or returns the backend failure. Repair takes the lock, re-inspects, confirms the branch through SCM, resolves provisioning, stages the sandbox branch as the fallback source, and calls create with `ReuseExisting`. Add the failure paths for a missing branch, a record without a branch, a backend that cannot be asked and a preparation refusal.","Create on an active or paused name returns conflict. Create on an orphan branch returns conflict and does not adopt it. A missing sandbox with a live branch is repaired through `ReuseExisting`. A missing branch returns unavailable with the delete-then-create remedy. A preparation refusal returns its structured provisioning failure. No repair creates or deletes a branch.","high","8-12h","T-001,T-002,T-003,T-004","ensure-live-or-repair,repair-is-create,repair-preserves-workspace,repair-failure,branch-missing,record-without-branch,preparation-refuses-during-repair"
  T-006,"[x] Implement bubblewrap reuse-mode create","Teach `BubblewrapBackend::create` about `CreateMode`. `Fresh` keeps the current conflict and copy-from-source path. `ReuseExisting` checks liveness through the pid probe: absent proceeds, live is conflict, no readable pid is unavailable with the delete remedy. Reuse an existing workspace; otherwise create it from the request source and mark it as materialised. Build the view and environment from the resolved request, start the holder, wait for readiness, apply limits, run sandbox steps only when the workspace was materialised, overwrite stale status and diagnostic files, and write the payload atomically after readiness. On failure tear down the holder and remove only a workspace this attempt created.","A dead v1 record with an existing workspace repairs in place and preserves workspace files. A missing workspace is materialised from the branch and the sandbox steps run. A reused workspace does not run the sandbox steps. A failed readiness or step run leaves the old payload and workspace and removes only the new holder. No repair reads the full v1 payload.","high","10-14h","T-002,T-005","repair-preserves-workspace,repair-rebuilds-environment,workspace-missing,setup-after-workspace-rebuild,stale-state-files,repair-spawn-fails,unreadable-payload-with-workspace"
  T-007,"[x] Report teardown facts from backend delete","Return `Teardown` from bubblewrap delete with the state directory and whether compute was stopped. A readable payload tears down a live sandbox and reports true. An unreadable or unsupported payload reports false with the reason and still removes the state directory. Adapt Docker and TestBackend to return their own teardown facts without changing their delete behaviour.","Delete returns the state paths bubblewrap removed. An unreadable payload returns compute_stopped false and the reason. Docker and TestBackend compile with the new return type. Existing delete idempotency tests pass.","medium","3-5h","T-001","delete-corrupt-record,corrupt-record-removable,unreadable-payload-delete-force"
  T-008,"[x] Refuse paused commands before the join","In `Sandboxes::exec`, inspect before the join. A paused sandbox returns `Error::Paused` and never reaches the backend exec. Upload, download and snapshot use the allow policy and continue because they do not join. Pause, resume, list and forwards keep their paths. Add a test that a paused exec performs no join and returns immediately.","A paused shell returns exit 4 and the resume command. A paused MCP command tool returns class conflict with the reason and remedy. Upload, download and snapshot still work on a paused sandbox. No backend exec is called for a paused sandbox.","low","2-4h","T-001,T-003","paused-refusal,paused-returns-immediately,paused-host-side-operations,repair-while-paused"
  T-009,"[x] Enumerate records first and report unknown","Add `metadata_store::entries_in` that returns every `.toml` record, including corrupt and unreadable files. Change `Sandboxes::list` to fill current and corrupt records first, sort by name, then enumerate branches and add only names with no record as orphans. Record a branch enumeration failure instead of dropping records. Change `inspect_listing` to return `InspectionReport`: a backend selection failure is Unknown for every record, a per-record refusal is Error, and only a successful inspect is Inspected.","A record without a branch appears in list. A branch without a record still appears as an orphan. A corrupt record is not reported as an orphan. A backend that cannot be selected reports every record as unknown and exits 1. A per-record refusal prints error, not unknown. Missing remains exit 0.","medium","5-7h","T-003","unknown-status,list-records-and-branches,list-shows-unpaired,list-without-backend,record-without-branch,orphan-branch,backend-unavailable"
  T-010,"[x] Implement delete confirmation and corrupt removal","Move the delete policy into `Sandboxes::delete(name, force)`. Inspect a current record: active, missing, unknown or error without force returns Denied with the record, workspace and branch names and the unmerged-work warning; paused keeps its current path. With force, delete compute, branch and record and return `Deletion`. A corrupt or unreadable record with force skips payload parsing, removes the record file and deterministic branch, calls the backend best-effort, and reports compute it could not stop.","Delete on missing without force exits 6 and names the record, workspace and branch. With force it removes them and prints what it removed. A corrupt record is removed with force and reports that compute could not be stopped. An unreadable payload delete without force is refused. A second delete succeeds. Paused delete keeps its current behaviour.","high","6-8h","T-003,T-007","delete-missing-force,delete-corrupt-record,delete-missing-needs-force,corrupt-record-removable,corrupt-delete-without-force,unreadable-payload-delete-force,paused-delete"
  T-011,"[x] Update the CLI surface","Pass `force` to `Sandboxes::delete` and print the `Deletion` fields. Render the record-first listing and the three inspection reports. Print the recovery warning to stderr before normal output. Update the `delete --force` help to cover active, missing and undetermined records and the unmerged-work risk. Keep every existing command and exit class except the documented delete confirmation.","`litterbox list` prints active, paused, missing, unknown, error, corrupt and orphan entries correctly. `litterbox shell` on a missing sandbox prints the warning and runs. `litterbox shell` on a paused sandbox exits 4. `litterbox delete` without force refuses missing and undetermined records with exit 6. No command is added.","medium","4-6h","T-008,T-009,T-010","paused-refusal,paused-class-parity,list-shows-unpaired,delete-missing-force,recovery-warning,no-new-surface,no-new-tool-or-verb"
  T-012,"[x] Add MCP recovery blocks and paused error data","Add a helper that appends `Recovery` as a second `ContentBlock::json` block. Make the command helpers return `Performed<T>` so a repair inside read, write, patch, ls, glob, grep or bash is not lost. Append the recovery block to those tools and to `sandbox-create` when the orchestrator reports it. Add `reason` and `remedy` to the paused error data. Keep the tool list and argument names unchanged.","A recovered bash, read, write, patch, ls, glob and grep result carries the normal content plus one recovery block. `sandbox-ports` never carries one. A paused command returns invalid params with class conflict, reason and remedy. The tool names and argument test still passes unchanged.","medium","6-8h","T-003,T-008","paused-class-parity,recovery-warning,cli-mcp-class-parity,no-new-surface,no-new-tool-or-verb"
  T-013,"[x] Wire create-on-missing through MCP","Make `sandbox-create` return `Performed<SandboxRecord>`. On a missing name it follows the repair path, returns the live inspection and carries the recovery block. On an active or paused name it returns conflict. On an orphan branch it returns conflict without adopting the branch.","`sandbox-create` on a missing name returns a live inspection plus a recovery block naming the branch and prior state. It does not create a second branch or record. Active, paused and orphan names return conflict.","medium","3-5h","T-005,T-012","create-on-missing,create-reports-recovery,create-active-or-paused,orphan-branch"
  T-014,"[x] Adapt Docker and TestBackend","Docker reports `ReuseExisting` as Unsupported with the delete-then-create remedy and returns `Teardown` from delete. TestBackend gains a missing state, records the `CreateMode` it received, counts exec calls, supports resurrection through `ReuseExisting`, and returns `Teardown`. Update the conformance suite and every fixture for the new signatures.","The conformance suite passes against TestBackend. Docker's existing tests pass unchanged. A missing TestBackend record repairs only through `ReuseExisting`. Docker on a missing name returns unsupported with the delete remedy, not a panic or a silent create.","medium","4-6h","T-001,T-003,T-007","backward-compatibility,repair-failure,backend-unavailable"
  T-015,"[x] Build the lifecycle matrix and incident regression tests","Add table-driven tests for every cell of the CLI and MCP matrices: active, paused, missing, corrupt and orphan records against list, shell, pause, resume, delete, the command tools, sandbox-ports and sandbox-create. Add the incident fixture: a current record, a live branch, a state directory with a workspace, dead pids and a v1 payload. Add tests for a branch that is gone, a record without a branch, a preparation refusal, a stale status file, an unreadable-payload delete without force, and two concurrent repairs. Add an ignored host test that creates a real bubblewrap sandbox, kills it, runs a command, and checks the workspace survived.","Every matrix cell has a named test. The v1 incident repairs and reports recovery with the workspace preserved. The branch-gone case returns the delete-then-create remedy. Concurrent repairs spawn one sandbox. The ignored host test passes where bubblewrap is available and names the missing requirement where it is not.","high","10-14h","T-005,T-006,T-008,T-009,T-010,T-013,T-014","test-matrix,matrix-tests,workspace-tests-recovers,concurrent-repair-single-holder,paused-returns-immediately,list-shows-unpaired,unreadable-payload-with-workspace,workspace-missing,branch-missing,state-directory-corrupt,backend-unavailable,concurrent-calls,repair-spawn-fails,orphan-branch,record-without-branch,paused-host-side-operations,paused-delete,create-active-or-paused,corrupt-delete-without-force,preparation-refuses-during-repair,list-without-backend,repair-while-paused,stale-state-files,setup-after-workspace-rebuild,unreadable-payload-delete-force"
  T-016,"[x] Update lifecycle docs and regenerate references","Update `lifecycle.mdx`: the state diagram, the CLI and MCP matrices, the failure-class table, the delete confirmation, corrupt removal and record-first listing. Mirror the operation tables and recovery prose in `src/docgen.rs`. Regenerate `reference/cli.mdx` and `reference/mcp.mdx` with the existing docgen commands. Add a docgen test that asserts the new rows and prose are present.","The lifecycle page states that missing repairs, paused refuses with conflict, delete on missing or undetermined needs force, corrupt records are removable with force, and forwards and sandbox-ports are record-only. Both generated reference pages contain the same tables and prose. The docgen test fails if a row or state is removed.","medium","3-5h","T-011,T-012,T-013","lifecycle-documentation,generated-documentation,reference-regenerated"
  T-017,"[x] Run final verification","Run `cargo test -p agentkit-litterbox` and `cargo clippy -p agentkit-litterbox --all-targets -- -D warnings`. Check the MCP tool list, the CLI command list and the generated reference pages for drift. Check that every spec slug appears in at least one task's refs.","Tests and clippy pass. The MCP tool list is unchanged. No command is added. The generated pages match a fresh docgen run. Every FR, NFR, AC and EC slug is referenced by at least one task.","low","1-2h","T-015,T-016","verification,tests-and-clippy,no-new-tool-or-verb"
  T-018,"[ ] Materialise repair from the sandbox branch","In `orchestrator/service.rs`, change `repair` to read `self.vcs.sandbox_tip(&workspace)` before `self.vcs.tip(&workspace)` and pass the chosen revision to `materialise`. Use the sandbox tip whenever it exists; fall back to the shared tip only when `sandbox_tip` returns `NotFound` and no resolution is open. A `NotFound` from `tip` alone does not block repair when the sandbox ref exists. Add `source` (`sandbox` or `shared`) and `fallback` to `Recovery`; `fallback` names `refs/litterbox/workspaces/<name>` when the shared tip was used. Serialise both in the MCP recovery block and include them in the CLI warning. Keep the existing `unavailable` remedy when both calls return `NotFound`. Extend `TestVcs` with absent `tip`/`sandbox_tip` and keep the materialise log.","A `Pending` sandbox with a live sandbox branch materialises the sandbox tip, not the shared tip. An absent sandbox branch materialises the shared tip and reports `source: shared` plus a `fallback`. A shared ref that is absent while the sandbox ref is live still repairs from the sandbox tip. Both absent returns the existing remedy. A sandbox ref equal to the shared tip reports `source: sandbox`. No repair creates a branch.","medium","3-5h","T-005","repair-source,repair-preserves-workspace,repair-failure,recovery-warning,workspace-missing,branch-missing,record-without-branch,sandbox-branch-absent,sandbox-branch-equals-tip,repair-preserves-sandbox-work"
  T-019,"[ ] Keep an open resolution through repair","Copy `stored.resolution` into the rewritten record in `repair`, as `merge` already is. Do not call `resolve_begin`, `set_sandbox_tip` or `set_tip`. When the sandbox revision cannot be read (Git `NotFound`, jj missing workspace) and a resolution is open, return `unavailable` with a reason naming the recorded `synced`/`ours`, instead of falling back to the shared tip. T-025 adds the shared VCS continuation.","A missing sandbox with an open resolution and a live sandbox branch repairs, keeps the resolution record unchanged, and the workspace holds the revision under resolution. An absent sandbox branch with an open resolution refuses, names the recorded revisions and does not clear the record. `finish` and `abandon` remain the only clearing operations.","low","2-3h","T-018","repair-open-resolution,open-resolution,resolution-without-sandbox-branch,repair-keeps-resolution,repair-preserves-sandbox-work"
  T-020,"[ ] Rename the source state to diverged and report it","Change the model-facing source state from `clean`/`held` to `clean`/`diverged`/`resolving` in `orchestrator/reconcile.rs`'s `WorkspaceBlock` and in `SourceStatus`. `diverged` holds when the record has a stored merge or the shared tip reports conflicts; `resolving` holds when `stored.resolution` is `Some` and wins over `diverged`. Add a `reason` to `SourceStatus` (and the MCP response) that names an unsaved-work divergence or a conflicted shared tip. `Sandboxes::list` adds the record's source state without inspecting the workspace, and `handle_list` prints it. Update the `WorkspaceBlock.reason` text to carry the same distinction. Leave the plan steps unchanged.","`sandbox-status` and every mutating tool's block report `clean`, `diverged` or `resolving`. A pending merge reports `diverged` with the unsaved-work reason; a conflicted shared tip reports `diverged` with the conflict reason; an open resolution reports `resolving`. `sandbox-status` carries that reason. `litterbox list` prints the source state from the record. No tool is refused in either state and the plan still snapshots to the sandbox branch.","medium","3-5h","T-018","source-state-matrix,source-state,commands-while-diverged,list-records-and-branches"
  T-021,"[ ] Refuse paused resolution actions and keep status answering","Add the paused check to `begin_resolution`, `finish_resolution` and `abandon_resolution` in `orchestrator/service.rs`, using the same `ensure_live(.., PausedPolicy::Refuse)` path as `exec`, before the resolver inspects or writes the workspace. Do not add the check to `source_status`.","`sandbox-reconcile` with `begin`, `finish` or `abandon` on a paused sandbox returns class `conflict` with the resume remedy and leaves the workspace and record untouched. `sandbox-status` still answers with the divergence and the open resolution. After `resume`, the same action proceeds.","low","2-3h","T-020","paused-refusal,paused-class-parity,paused-returns-immediately,paused-reconcile,paused-host-side-operations,repair-while-paused"
  T-022,"[ ] Replace --force with per-condition delete guards","Change `Sandboxes::delete(name, force)` to take `DeleteGuards { running, invalid, unmerged }` and wire `--ignore-running`, `--ignore-invalid` and `--ignore-unmerged` through `cli.rs`; remove `--force`. Each guard is checked and reported independently, and a refusal names every flag the record needs plus the record, both branches and any staging workspace. `paused` and `missing` set no running guard. The unmerged guard holds when the sandbox tip is not an ancestor of the shared tip, the shared ref is absent while the sandbox ref exists, a resolution is open, or a staging workspace exists. Extend `Deletion` with the refs, the staging workspace and the guards whose flags were unused, and print them. Update the `delete` help to describe each guard, and update Docker's `ReuseExisting` unsupported remedy to name the delete flags instead of `--force`. This supersedes the `--force` policy from T-010 and T-011.","An active sandbox needs `--ignore-running`; a corrupt or undetermined record needs `--ignore-invalid`; a diverged sandbox, an open resolution or a staging workspace needs `--ignore-unmerged`. Missing and paused need no compute flag. Passing one flag does not satisfy another. The refusal names all required flags, the record, both branches and any staging workspace. With the flags, delete removes staging, compute, the shared branch, the sandbox branch, the synced ref and the record and prints them; a passed flag whose condition did not hold is reported as unused. `--force` is gone and its use is a clap error.","high","5-8h","T-020","delete-missing-force,delete-corrupt-record,delete-missing-needs-force,corrupt-record-removable,corrupt-delete-without-force,unreadable-payload-delete-force,paused-delete,several-delete-guards,unused-delete-flag,backward-compatibility,no-new-surface,repair-failure,backend-unavailable"
  T-023,"[ ] Build the source-state and delete-guard matrix tests","Extend the table-driven tests with the source states `clean`, `diverged` and `resolving` against `list`, `shell` and the MCP command tools, `pause`, `resume`, `delete`, `sandbox-create`, `sandbox-status`, `sandbox-reconcile`, repair and the absent-sandbox status. Include a `Pending` repair that materialises the sandbox branch and preserves its work, a paused `sandbox-reconcile` refusal for each action, and one test per delete guard and per combination. Add the incident fixture with a live shared branch and a different live sandbox branch.","Every new matrix cell has a named test. The `Pending` repair preserves the sandbox branch work and reports `source: sandbox`. A paused `begin`, `finish` and `abandon` each return `conflict` without touching the workspace. The absent-sandbox status returns the recorded revisions and the continuation, and repair refuses with the same text. Each delete guard refuses alone and combines with the others. The matrix test fails when a cell loses its test.","high","8-10h","T-018,T-019,T-020,T-021,T-022,T-025","test-matrix,matrix-tests,workspace-tests-recovers,repair-preserves-sandbox-work,commands-while-diverged,paused-reconcile,several-delete-guards,unused-delete-flag,delete-missing-needs-force,absent-sandbox-revision"
  T-024,"[ ] Update lifecycle docs and regenerate both references","Update `docs/docs/user/litterbox/lifecycle.mdx` with the state diagram, the compute and source state tables, a second matrix over `clean`, `diverged` and `resolving`, the repair-source rule and its fallback, the absent-sandbox status and continuation, the paused `sandbox-reconcile` refusal, and the three delete flags. Mirror the tables and prose in `src/docgen.rs`, then regenerate `reference/cli.mdx` and `reference/mcp.mdx` with the existing docgen commands. Add docgen assertions for the new rows and for the removed `held`/`--force` words.","The lifecycle page distinguishes compute state from source state, states that repair materialises the sandbox branch and reports the shared fallback, reports an absent sandbox revision with the recorded revisions and the reflog/op-log continuation, refuses paused `sandbox-reconcile`, and documents each delete guard. Both generated pages contain the same tables and prose. A docgen test fails if a row, state or flag is removed.","medium","3-5h","T-018,T-019,T-020,T-021,T-022,T-025","lifecycle-documentation,generated-documentation,reference-regenerated"
  T-025,"[ ] Report an absent sandbox revision in status","Add a shared continuation helper in `orchestrator/` that, for a sandbox with an open resolution, names the recorded `synced`/`ours`, the VCS store from `Vcs::state_path`, and the Git (`fsck --lost-found`, `update-ref`) or jj (`op log`, `workspace add`) recovery, identifying the resolution commit by its two parents (`ours` and the shared tip). Make `SourceStatus` carry `sandbox: Option<String>`, `ours: Option<String>` and `next: Option<String>`, and `Report` carry `sandbox: Option<Revision>` and `next: Option<String>`. In `source_status` and `report`, catch the sandbox-revision failure only when a resolution is open and return `resolving`, `sandbox: None`, the recorded revisions and the continuation; propagate every other error. Print `sandbox absent` and `next` in `handle_status`, and return the same fields from `sandbox-status`.","With an open resolution and no sandbox revision, `litterbox status` and `sandbox-status` return `resolving`, `sandbox: null`, the recorded `synced`/`ours` and `next`; repair refuses with the same `next`. A missing sandbox revision with no open resolution is still an error. No ref is written. Git and jj tests cover the helper.","medium","4-6h","T-019,T-020","absent-sandbox-revision,resolution-without-sandbox-branch,repair-open-resolution,source-state-matrix,open-resolution"
  T-026,"[ ] Run final verification for the amendment","Run `cargo test -p agentkit-litterbox`, `cargo clippy -p agentkit-litterbox --all-targets -- -D warnings`, `arch-lint check` and `bash hack/arch-lint-negative.sh`. Check the MCP tool list, the CLI command list, the generated pages and every spec slug against the tasks.","Tests, clippy and both arch-lint gates pass. The MCP tool list is unchanged. No command is added. `--force` and `held` no longer appear on a user-facing surface. Every FR, NFR, AC and EC slug is referenced by at least one task.","low","1-2h","T-023,T-024,T-025","verification,tests-and-clippy,no-new-tool-or-verb"
